  "title": "Quick reference of <code class=\"code-inline tex2jax_ignore\">ArrayList<\/code> methods",
  "body": " Quick reference of ArrayList methods       ArrayList Method  What It Does  Standard Array Equivalent    list.size()  Returns the number of elements currently stored in the list.  count (tracked manually; arr.length is fixed capacity)    list.add(item)  Appends item to the end of the list.  arr[count] = item; count++; (if count < arr.length )    list.add(index, item)  Inserts item at index , shifting existing elements right.  Manual right-shift loop + insert + count++;    list.get(index)  Returns the element at index .  arr[index]    list.set(index, item)  Replaces the element at index with item and returns the previous value.  arr[index] = item;    list.remove(index)  Removes and returns the element at index , shifting subsequent elements left.  Manual left-shift loop + count--;    list.remove(item)  Removes the first matching element (via .equals() ), returning true if found.  Manual search + left-shift loop + count--;    "
